   "notes": "Chapel of St John Fisher (Catholic Chaplaincy), facing Fisher Square: 1980s buff brick. Left (south-west) part a gabled hall with a dark-framed projecting box window and a strip of small clerestory windows under the eaves; right part the chapel block, blank buff brick below a continuous band of tall timber-framed clerestory glazing under a hipped slate roof with cross finial. Window counts from the geograph view; positions estimated."
